WEBVTT

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:04.020
Hi! I'm Yukkyun.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.210
The show has finally 
passed the halfway point.

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:10.390
That means this'll be the 
last of this segment.

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:13.840
So it'll be extra special!

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.200
I call it Penalty Time!

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.930
<i>What? What's that about a penalty?</i>

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.930
Yay!

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:21.930
<i>How can you give us penalties if 
there hasn't even been a contest?</i>

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:27.100
In this segment, I randomly choose someone 
to receive the penalty I come up with.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.020
<i>You can't do that!</i>

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.000
It's a simple segment.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.000
<i>That's absurd!</i>

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.610
<i>Ridiculous!</i>

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.570
What should the first penalty be?

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.570
<i>Someone stop her!</i>

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.050
Let's make it something sexy
 since we air after midnight.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:41.480
<i>What is she saying?</i>

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:44.120
<i>Quick, stop her!</i>

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.790
How about...

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:50.020
dragging the camera all over the chosen 
person's nude body from bottom to top?

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:50.020
<i>Is she really Nagi-chan's mother?</i>

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.960
<i>Um, yes.</i>

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:54.320
Find out who gets penalized 
at the end of the show!

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.240
<i>What? She's really gonna 
do that to someone?</i>

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:57.600
And there won't be some lame punchline

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.960
<i>Not to me!</i>

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.730
like Claus being naked, 
so look forward to it!

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.450
<i>Nobody wants to see that anyway.</i>

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:02.790
<i>What?</i>

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:06.050
Nothing.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:07.090
I had nothing.

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:10.110
My life was full of nothing.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:17.130
That's why I desperately wanted 
things other people had.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.490
<i>Thief!</i>

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:21.060
That's why I stole things.

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:24.680
To give my life worth.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:26.850
I took everything I could.

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.270
I robbed and robbed 
and robbed everyone.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:34.870
But still, I was left 
with nothing tangible.

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:36.900
I was at a loss.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.280
That's when I met you.

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:45.600
I became your butler.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.420
I only did as I was told in order 
to steal the black camellia.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:53.500
I lived a lie every day 
just for the chance...

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:55.420
Or so I thought.

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:03.180
But this became the best 
part of my shitty life.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.340
<i>You'll do as the man of my dreams.</i>

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:12.330
After a while, I no longer wanted 
you to think, "You'll do."

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:16.990
I wanted you to say, "I'm glad 
you're the man of my dreams."

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:19.640
"I will never betray you..."

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:22.150
...was the promise I made,

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.170
as we exchanged our rings 
and our eternal love.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.870
The man who betrayed Yukariko...

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.840
...and stole the black camellia...

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:36.590
<i>It was your father, Shin Hayek.</i>

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:14.840
So this is the Reitaisai convention that 
has nothing to do with Touhou?

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:17.650
What exactly are you comparing this to?

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:19.940
Hey, cotton candy!

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.920
Hayate, Hayate! Buy me some!

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:26.740
What? Maria-san will 
get mad at you again.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.690
Don't tell and she won't know.

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:29.490
Yeah, but...

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:32.130
There's something irresistible 
about cotton candy,

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:34.120
particularly the bags.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:35.470
Look.

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:37.880
<b> Heisei 15</b>

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.490
Even a poor girl like Tsugumi is agonizing

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:44.950
over whether or not to spend 
what little money she has on it.

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:49.130
Hey, Tsugumi! Is that wise?

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:47.410
<i>Right...</i>

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:50.760
Wh-What?

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:55.280
Is this really a good time for you 
to be extravagant with money?

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.270
<i>The black camellia was found?</i>

00:04:58.640 --> 00:04:59.680
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.850
<i>The Las Vegas Police Department 
in America has it...</i>

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:04.280
<i>...with my late father's things.</i>

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:06.660
<i>A-America.</i>

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.040
<i>They'll chuck it if I don't</i>

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:10.720
<i>collect it within three days.</i>

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:13.380
<i>Th-Then hurry!</i>

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:14.280
<i>No.</i>

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:14.910
<i>Why?</i>

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:18.920
<i>It's something my father stole 
from my mother. It's garbage.</i>

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:23.420
<i>I want every trace of 
it gone from this earth.</i>

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:25.510
<i>If it's garbage, then give it to me!</i>

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:28.310
<i>No. Why should I go all the way</i>

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.180
<i>to America just to give it to you?</i>

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:34.680
<i>By the way, security is really tight at 
the Las Vegas Police Department.</i>

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:36.440
<i>It's impossible to steal it.</i>

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:40.690
<i>The black camellia won't be 
released unless I go get it.</i>

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:44.540
<i>It'll be gone in three days. Give up!</i>

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:45.320
<i>And...</i>

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:46.820
<i>And?</i>

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:50.570
<i>You don't have money to buy 
a ticket to America, right?</i>

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:55.000
If you wanna blame something, 
blame your poorness.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:00.500
Um, speaking of that... 
Nishizawa-san said she's entering this.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:00.500
<b> Special Festival Event</b>

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:00.500
<b><i>Win a ticket to New York 
by answering quiz questions!!</i></b>

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:05.010
Does anyone want to go to New York?

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.510
Yeah!

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:10.170
What's this?

00:06:10.170 --> 00:06:15.030
If you win, you get airline 
tickets to America.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:21.020
Tickets to America, yeah,
 but to New York.

00:06:21.020 --> 00:06:23.230
This is my last chance.

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:25.900
Nishizawa-san.

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:28.160
I'm winning this contest

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:31.180
so I can go see Ruka live in Las Vegas!

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:32.120
<i>Glitter!</i>

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:36.220
You're going to win 
tickets to New York...

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:38.120
...and then go to Las Vegas?

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:42.100
New York and Las Vegas 
are both in America.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:44.880
After getting to New York, 
I figured I could...

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:49.620
...hop on the Shinkansen or 
whatever and zoom over to Vegas.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:50.760
Right?

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.080
<i>Is she serious?</i>

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:56.340
I see. What a brilliant idea!

00:06:56.340 --> 00:06:58.560
Hee, hee. Right?

00:06:58.560 --> 00:06:59.850
Vroom!

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:03.980
Is Las Vegas that close to New York?

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:09.240
Well... I think they're a bit 
closer than Tokyo and India.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:12.550
I also have to ride this big wave.

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:15.390
Where's registration?

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:18.620
<i>Oh, but this says you need a partner.</i>

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.620
<b> Place: Quiz Plaza</b>

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.620
<b> Registration: Open until dusk</b>

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.620
<b> To Qualify: Register in pairs!</b>

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.270
Come on, big sister!

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:22.330
What?! Hey!

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.770
Why do I have to be your 
partner in this stupid contest?

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:27.340
<i>Does it matter?</i>

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.010
Yes, it does!

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:31.970
I have to get the black camellia!

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:35.470
So...

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:39.980
Do you even know what 
the black camellia is?

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:41.100
Huh?

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:45.860
The old geezer said it's a 
clock that brings bad luck.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.230
It brings... bad luck?

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.370
The black camellia... a clock that destroys

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:54.220
the owner's fortune and brings them bad luck.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:57.060
Anyone who obtains it gets cursed.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:02.500
Who would want a clock 
that brings bad luck?

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:05.640
<i>There's another legend.</i>

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:06.760
A legend?

00:08:07.290 --> 00:08:10.410
<i>The black camellia measures all 
of eternity in alternation.</i>

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:13.210
<i>If someone can overcome its 
bad luck with their life intact...</i>

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:16.580
<i>...then the owner of the clock will 
obtain the miracle of all miracles...</i>

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.390
...when both hands on 
the clock strike eight.

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:20.690
Miracle?

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:23.560
<i>As a reward for overcoming
 the black camellia's curse...</i>

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.290
<i>...they'll obtain unbelievable
 luck in return.</i>

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:30.090
<i>If you play the slots, 
you'll definitely win big.</i>

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:34.020
But no one has ever been 
able to confirm this.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:38.870
So far, everyone's been 
crushed by bad luck first.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:45.420
I... I still have to get hold 
of the black camellia.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:46.840
You...

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:49.590
You must have been tricked.

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.670
What's that supposed to mean?

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:53.230
Well, you're stupid.

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:54.720
What?

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:56.380
Whatever.

00:08:56.380 --> 00:08:58.490
But I'll say this much:

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:01.430
If you're planning 
something bad, just stop.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:03.350
It doesn't suit you.

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:07.340
What? Are you saying 
I can't do anything?

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:08.650
No.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.780
I still don't know who you really are.

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:16.650
But if you claim to be my 
little sister, that's fine.

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:17.530
Huh?

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.700
I won't try to uncover your identity.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.160
I won't question you either.

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:26.540
If you say you're my little 
sister, I believe you.

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:30.420
This is advice from your big sister.

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:34.390
Don't do anything dangerous.

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:37.110
You don't need a clock that 
brings bad luck, do you?

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:40.550
But...

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:43.300
I...

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:46.790
<i>Registration for the quiz will end soon.</i>

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:49.810
<i>Please hurry if you want to participate.</i>

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:52.780
You really are hopeless.

00:09:53.090 --> 00:09:53.860
Huh?

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:56.540
I think we register over there.

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.220
Oh, okay.

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:03.370
You have terrible handwriting.

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:06.270
Shut up! Don't look.

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:09.020
Hey! Hayate, Hayate!

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:11.880
What is it, Miss Nagi?

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:15.380
<b>Connecting</b>

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:15.380
<b>Theater</b>

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:15.380
<b>Part A</b>

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:22.870
<b><i> Ruri Tsugumi</i></b>

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:18.160
Take a look at Tsugumi's handwriting.

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:21.980
Whoa. It's awfully crooked.

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:25.520
Your handwriting reflects your nature.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.920
So <i>that</i> must be what 
Tsugumi is really like.

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:31.770
Oh yeah? Then let's see <i>you</i>
 write something, big sister!

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:35.320
<b> Nagi Sanzenin</b>

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:34.740
Sorry, I have perfect handwriting.

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:38.190
Were you expecting some 
kind of funny punchline?

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:41.320
I guess a person's handwriting doesn't 
reflect their nature after all.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:42.390
Of course.

00:10:42.390 --> 00:10:43.670
What?

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:47.710
<b>Connecting</b>

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:47.710
<b>Theater</b>

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:47.710
<b>Part B</b>

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:51.710
<i>Let's start the preliminary 
round of the quiz competition!</i>

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:54.480
At least she does stuff like that right.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:56.960
<i>Okay, question one! Ta-da!</i>

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:59.970
<i>Fumi is feeling very "ennui" today.</i>

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:01.070
Huh?

00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:02.720
Who cares?!

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:06.050
<i>Let's begin Torauma Town's</i>

00:11:06.050 --> 00:11:09.660
<i>One Way Ticket to America Ultra Quiz!</i>

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:14.390
<i>Here are the contestants!</i>

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:18.780
They're all people we know.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:21.580
Well, it is a neighborhood event.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:34.630
Yikes. We're surrounded by 
fierce contestants, Hina-san.

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:39.160
Even if we win, I'm 
not going to New York.

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:42.570
Why? Why not, Hina-san?

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:45.930
I don't want to go on an airplane.

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:49.020
Why are Isumi and Sakuya competing?

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:50.930
Why would they need plane tickets?

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:54.190
I don't need the tickets,

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:56.130
but it seemed like something we could win,

00:11:56.130 --> 00:11:57.890
so we just entered to beat everyone.

00:11:57.890 --> 00:12:00.690
Sorry it's such a weird reason.

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:03.280
Who are they?

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:06.010
Isumi Saginomiya and Sakuya Aizawa.

00:12:06.010 --> 00:12:07.200
They're my friends.

00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:18.060
<i>Quiz time! Things are getting exciting!</i>

00:12:18.060 --> 00:12:23.090
<i>Which pair will win the 
one way tickets to America?</i>

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:21.700
<b> One Way</b>

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:23.090
<b> Only to go there.</b>

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:25.830
It's only one way?

00:12:25.830 --> 00:12:27.350
Looks like it.

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:33.100
<i>Let's begin with the 
first fateful question.</i>

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:34.600
<i>Buzz in first to answer!</i>

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:40.600
<i>When Fumi got home, her mother 
was kissing a stranger.</i>

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:41.240
<i>Why?</i>

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:43.480
"Why"?!

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:46.240
Are we allowed to 
answer such a question?

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:47.150
I know!

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:49.280
<i>Isumi Saginomiya-san! You're fast.</i>

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:50.450
<i>Go ahead!</i>

00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:54.520
Your mother loves men.

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.470
<i>She said it.</i>

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:00.840
<i>Close! Be more specific!</i>

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:03.520
<i>Is it okay to be more specific?</i>

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:05.590
I know!

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:07.300
<i>Yes, Nishizawa-san.</i>

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:09.030
She's having an affair.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:11.720
<i>Ding, ding, ding, ding! You are correct!</i>

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:14.100
<i>That's the correct response?!</i>

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:17.480
Is this quiz tournament going to be all right?

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:18.860
I-I have no idea.

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:20.830
<i>Question two.</i>

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:22.390
<i>Find what's wrong.</i>

00:13:22.390 --> 00:13:24.210
This is where I get serious.

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:25.860
Uh... Yeah.

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:28.940
<i>There's something wrong with this picture.</i>

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:30.870
<i>What's the mistake?</i>

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:35.390
<b> I'm leaving you.</b>

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:35.390
<b> I'm also suing you.</b>

00:13:33.680 --> 00:13:35.390
<b> Makie</b>

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:39.650
<b> Husband: Kunimasa Hibino</b>

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:39.650
<b> Wife: Makie Hibino</b>

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:42.400
<b> I'm leaving you.</b>

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:42.400
<b> I'm also suing you.</b>

00:13:39.690 --> 00:13:42.400
<b> Makie</b>

00:13:44.890 --> 00:13:46.720
<i>Th-The mistake...</i>

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:49.490
<i>I can't tell what 
the mistake is, Makie.</i>

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:53.220
The names are wrong?

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:54.750
<i>Nope!</i>

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:56.850
<i>That is incorrect. 
This document is real.</i>

00:13:57.320 --> 00:13:58.850
<i>It's real?</i>

00:13:59.320 --> 00:14:00.790
<i>It's real...</i>

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.150
<i>Whoa, Isumi-san!</i>

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.520
You've got an answer?

00:14:06.080 --> 00:14:07.110
<i>Cough.</i>

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:10.170
It's wrong because your mom

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:11.990
had the affair, but says she's suing.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:15.130
<i>Ding, ding, ding, ding! 
That's correct!</i>

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:16.370
<i>And that's the correct response?</i>

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:19.140
<i>Finally, we have a true or false question.</i>

00:14:19.140 --> 00:14:21.290
<i>It's worth three points.</i>

00:14:21.710 --> 00:14:24.340
<i>Press that buzzer quickly!</i>

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:28.050
<i>Fumi's house is currently a battleground.</i>

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:30.050
True.

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:31.080
<i>Correct!</i>

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:35.660
<b> Winner!!</b>

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:35.430
<i>Nishizawa-san's team wins!</i>

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:39.200
Yay! I'm so excited!

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:42.560
We can go to America, Hina-san!

00:14:43.630 --> 00:14:44.910
I'm so frustrated!

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:46.440
It's okay.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:47.650
Why?

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.880
Now you have to give up.

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:52.690
Forget about the black camellia.

00:14:56.060 --> 00:14:59.240
It's just not that simple!

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:01.190
Hey, Tsugumi!

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:04.550
Nagi, who's that?

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:08.060
That's my troublesome little sister.

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:15.310
Hayate, take care of Tsugumi.

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:16.570
Of course.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:20.690
<b> Prize</b>

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:23.030
Yay! Now we can go see Ruka's concert.

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:26.190
<b>Yakisoba - Giant Servings</b>

00:15:20.690 --> 00:15:26.190
<b> Rich Morokoshi</b>

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:24.450
Right, Hina-san?

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:26.190
Y-Yes.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:28.070
What's wrong?

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:30.450
Um... Um...

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:32.570
It's an airplane!

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:36.290
It'll be okay. I'll hold 
your hand the whole time.

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:38.790
That's not the problem!

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:41.620
Did you see the music video, Hina-san?

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:48.420
It looks like the concert staging will 
be based on a forest legend motif.

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:50.670
It's really beautiful.

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:03.700
This is a story from long, long ago,
in a land far, far away.

00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:10.680
Beside a beautiful forest and lake

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:12.700
stood a small castle.

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:22.190
By the lakeside, there lived 
an apple tree nymph.

00:16:24.100 --> 00:16:27.490
The nymph fell in love with the prince

00:16:27.490 --> 00:16:29.650
who lived in the castle.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:37.280
The two lost track of time talking.

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:40.640
They talked about things that 
made them happy and sad.

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:45.790
For the prince, the nymph was 
the only one he could confide in.

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:51.360
For the nymph, these were 
also very happy times.

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:55.270
She stayed close and 
did everything for him.

00:16:57.210 --> 00:16:59.850
She granted every wish the prince had...

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:04.150
...because she loved him so much.

00:17:14.250 --> 00:17:17.360
Unlike a nymph, who can 
live for hundreds of years,

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:19.820
a human's life is short.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:24.440
Eventually, the end of their 
time together drew near.

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:36.070
The prince asked her 
to grant another wish:

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:38.820
He wanted to live forever.

00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:42.250
The nymph was torn.

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:46.520
But she couldn't ignore the wish of

00:17:46.520 --> 00:17:48.210
the prince she loved so much.

00:18:14.390 --> 00:18:16.590
She gave the prince life.

00:18:18.230 --> 00:18:23.500
She continued to grant him life, 
just as he wished...

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:31.440
In exchange for countless futures cut short.

00:18:58.060 --> 00:19:00.910
<i>I still don't know who you really are.</i>

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:05.590
<i>But if you claim to be my little sister...</i>

00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:06.700
<i>...that's fine.</i>

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:15.120
Big sister.

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:22.110
<i>What are you doing, Tsugumi?</i>

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:26.030
<i>The black camellia.</i>

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:30.310
<i>That is what you are here to obtain.</i>

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:32.430
Um, but...

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:35.750
<i>You haven't forgotten, have you?</i>

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:43.530
<i>This is advice from your big sister.</i>

00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:45.780
<i>Don't do anything dangerous.</i>

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:50.000
I'm sorry, I don't have a single lead.

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:54.710
Who's there?

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:57.710
That's my line.

00:19:58.700 --> 00:20:00.690
Who are you guys?

00:20:00.690 --> 00:20:02.720
Why do you try to get close to Nagi?

00:20:03.190 --> 00:20:05.350
You're... Isumi Saginomiya.

00:20:20.270 --> 00:20:24.240
Hey, Isumi-san! What was that noise?

00:20:24.580 --> 00:20:25.740
Sakuya.

00:20:28.170 --> 00:20:29.410
Sakuya, get down!

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:40.100
What's with this wind?

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:41.490
I have no idea.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:49.850
Th-This is...

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:54.690
It's time to end this game of house.

00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:59.470
If Nagi Sanzenin needs 
to go to Las Vegas

00:20:59.470 --> 00:21:02.360
for her or Nagi to retrieve 
the black camellia...

00:21:02.850 --> 00:21:05.740
...then it is your job to get her there.

00:21:06.630 --> 00:21:08.120
Th-That's...

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:20.000
Tsugumi-san?

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:26.640
What's wrong, Tsugumi-san?

00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:41.980
Tsugumi-san!

00:23:18.720 --> 00:23:20.720
You thought I was a cute girl?

00:23:21.410 --> 00:23:22.430
You were right!

00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:24.960
I'm Yukkyun.

00:23:25.480 --> 00:23:29.300
See ya! Bye-bye!

00:23:30.850 --> 00:23:33.350
What the heck was that?

00:23:33.350 --> 00:23:35.710
Is this segment really ending?

00:23:35.710 --> 00:23:37.730
I might not appear anymore.

00:23:37.730 --> 00:23:38.980
Who knows.
